{"title":"2021 WSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c16df895dad08efcc67a9a5d66f8eb08a7c37e8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DEFG$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> be squares that intersect exactly once and with areas <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/5/cb510ebb5a173d1db97abcf03fcbccec0e73fba8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1011^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/9/1795e7534be689202f699b608f6befe8e7d34c69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$69^2$\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" /> respectively. There exists a constant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54c369182ae32ef4440bf2531b4598e7a02c08c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE+AG&gt;M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"125\" height=\"16\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is maximized. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195f17785e62de6d33f35a9ed2dee039dff256f1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(320); import olympiad;  pair A = (0,2); pair B = (2,2); pair C = (2,0); pair D = (0,0); pair E = rotate(120)*(0,1); pair F = rotate(120)*(1,1); pair G = rotate(120)*(1,0);  draw(A--B--C--D--cycle, black+linewidth(1)); draw(D--E--F--G--cycle, black+linewidth(1)); filldraw(A--B--C--D--cycle, lightgreen, black); filldraw(D--E--F--G--cycle, lightgreen, black);  draw(C--E, blue+linewidth(1.2)); draw(A--G, blue+linewidth(1.2));  label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, N); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, N); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, NE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, NE); label(&quot;$E$&quot;, E, SW); label(&quot;$F$&quot;, F, N); label(&quot;$G$&quot;, G, NW); [/asy]\" width=\"535\" height=\"415\" /> </center><p> We wish to the find the minimum value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/1/181389a62ef8d43d7c8d9076ae155735bc1d821b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE+AG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"81\" height=\"16\" />. For simplicity, let the sidelength of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/e/aaebf29087ee9f889b46925485853399bcd6b4a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=1011$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" /> and the sidelength of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c16df895dad08efcc67a9a5d66f8eb08a7c37e8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DEFG$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/9/6093a1e822645e59c57109ba8a38af277022b4b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=69$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/2/202fc7eef52767de0d67520164aaa8d74db8835c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(\\angle GDA)=-\\cos(\\angle EDC)=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"268\" height=\"20\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52ebe6de79419fad5a4cc599c58421f8140a8e18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in[-1,1]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"85\" height=\"20\" />. From the Law of Cosines, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/a/f3ab6e63bb88ad5fdd7c972f213f537a91045537.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[CE+AG=\\sqrt{a^2+b^2+2abx}+\\sqrt{a^2+b^2-2abx}.\\]\" width=\"386\" height=\"18\" /> We have  \\begin{align*} (CE+AG)^2&amp;=(a^2+b^2+2abx)+(a^2+b^2-2abx)+\\sqrt{(a^2+b^2+2abx)(a^2+b^2-2abx)}\\\\ &amp;=2(a^2+b^2)+\\sqrt{(a^2+b^2)^2-(2abx)^2}. \\end{align*} since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/6/cf669d58fbd0410ca860758e53606d06425a4d97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"16\" /> is fixed, this expression is minimized when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/2/5629b249172fead396bec70ace760823628d940d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2abx)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"60\" height=\"21\" /> is maximized, or when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/6/fb68c7179a2b0ca3a7e8758dadd1c5314d1e52ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\pm1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />. When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/6/fb68c7179a2b0ca3a7e8758dadd1c5314d1e52ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\pm1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/c/64c1fde6df848605aa5d99c21f3165507edb0d43.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[CE+AG=\\sqrt{a^2+b^2+2ab}+\\sqrt{a^2+b^2-2ab} = (a+b)+(a-b)=2a=\\boxed{2022}.\\]\" width=\"593\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>~pinkpig\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018020457\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.012 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.022 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 90/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4673/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:26404:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018020457 and revision id 274613. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}